From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vipul Cariappa <vipulcariappa@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 19:48:58 +0530
Subject: Drive the `%%python` magic with cppjit

cppyy's role here -- reflecting the kernel's own translation unit into
Python -- is now cppjit's, and cppjit attaches to the interpreter
CppInterOp already holds rather than creating one, which is what makes the
magic share state with the C++ cells around it.

Also fix the CppInterOp include to the current `CppInterOp/CppInterOp.h`
path; the old `clang/Interpreter/` location no longer exists.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit e7d39debdba4b35813354935318b1b0a9a41ff3e)
---
 src/xmagics/pythonexec.cpp | 14 ++++++++------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/xmagics/pythonexec.cpp b/src/xmagics/pythonexec.cpp
index fe85688..5a7bfc0 100644
--- a/src/xmagics/pythonexec.cpp
+++ b/src/xmagics/pythonexec.cpp
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@
 
 #include "Python.h"
 
-#include "clang/Interpreter/CppInterOp.h"
+#include "CppInterOp/CppInterOp.h"
 
 namespace xcpp {
     bool pythonexec::is_initalized = false;
@@ -69,17 +69,19 @@ namespace xcpp {
 
         PyRun_SimpleString("import sys\nsys.path.append('')"); // add current directory to PYTHONPATH
 
-        // Import cppyy module
-        PyObject* cppyyModule = PyImport_ImportModule("cppyy");
-        if (!cppyyModule) {
+        // cppjit binds against whichever interpreter CppInterOp already has,
+        // so importing it here hands the Python side this kernel's own
+        // translation unit rather than a fresh one.
+        PyObject* cppjitModule = PyImport_ImportModule("cppjit");
+        if (!cppjitModule) {
             PyErr_Print();
             Py_Finalize();
             return; // Handle import error as needed
         }
 
         PyObject* mainModule = PyImport_AddModule("__main__");
-        PyObject_SetAttrString(mainModule, "cppyy", cppyyModule);
-        Py_XDECREF(cppyyModule);
+        PyObject_SetAttrString(mainModule, "cppjit", cppjitModule);
+        Py_XDECREF(cppjitModule);
 
         is_initalized = true;
     }
